 ## 2026-08-10
 
+### 2112 — libssh2 teardown reconciles reserved races and late automatic-task retirement (TASK-260715-1ozsb6)
+- ROOT CAUSE: A reserved timeout race resumed teardown after its first child resolved but remained registered until both children retired. Teardown exposed completion without draining that registry, and it did not arrange durable automatic-task retirement until after socket close; if a cancellation-ignoring socket consumed the close deadline, the join branch was skipped and completed automatic-task references remained permanently counted.
+- REWORK: Automatic-task retirement now starts before socket close and clears actor-owned references only after every cancelled task actually returns. The reserved registry is drained within the existing close deadline, so cooperative races reconcile before completion while genuinely non-cooperative socket work remains visible until its safe late return.
+- CONFORMANCE: A connected OpenSSH regression starts with both automatic schedulers active, holds socket close past the 50 ms transport deadline while ignoring cancellation, proves bounded close, exact-once socket close, repeated-close safety, detached ownership visibility, and eventual zero sessions/channels/sockets/tasks/allocations/buffers after release. The formerly intermittent repeated-handshake cleanup passed 10 consecutive focused runs.
+- VERIFICATION: `swift test --filter LibSSH2` passes 41 tests/3 suites; `make validate-core` passes 375 tests/31 suites plus boundary checks and build; `make validate-libssh2`, `make test-libssh2-source-gates`, `make native-apple-matrix`, strict Swift format, `swift build`, and diff checks all exit 0. Board validation exits 0 with only the expected story aggregate mismatch while this task remains in development.
+
 ### 2053 — libssh2 socket teardown has capacity independent of ordinary operation pressure (TASK-260715-1ozsb6)
 - ROOT CAUSE: Socket close used the same 64-slot timeout-race registry as ordinary injected and channel work. Teardown cancelled that registry and immediately tried to register close; while cancellation-ignoring children still occupied all slots, admission failed and `try?` skipped `SSHTCPConnection.close()` before dropping the connection reference.
 - REWORK: Teardown now owns a separate fixed two-slot registry: one slot for the socket-close deadline and one for the automatic-task join deadline. Reserved admission is non-throwing under the single teardown owner, so ordinary saturation cannot bypass exact-once socket close; unfinished teardown children remain visible in the owned-resource snapshot until they retire.
