+# TASK-260715-1ozsb6 developer handoff — review-round-9 rework
+
+Status: ready for review.
+
+## Outcome
+
+- The pinned static libssh2/OpenSSL adapter remains isolated behind the candidate-neutral Core boundary and registered in the macOS provider and harness graphs.
+- Closed the round-9 lifecycle defect: automatic-task retirement now starts before socket close can consume the transport-close deadline, and actor-owned references clear only after the cancelled tasks actually retire.
+- Cooperative reserved timeout races are reconciled before teardown completion within the existing deadline. Genuinely non-cooperative work remains counted in the ownership snapshot until its safe late completion.
+- Added a connected OpenSSH regression with both automatic schedulers active and a cancellation-ignoring socket close. It proves bounded close, exact-once socket close, repeated-close safety, no optimistic ownership baseline, safe late completion, and eventual zero sessions, channels, sockets, tasks, custom allocations, and buffers.
+- Preserved bounded nonblocking EAGAIN integration, privacy-safe errors, Keychain-only opaque credentials/external signing, host verification before credential lookup, direct-tcpip, exec/stdin upload, client/server rekey behavior, keepalive transmission, and available metrics.
+- The four M3-deferred semantics remain explicit `unsupported`/`notReported` states owned by `TASK-260728-3cveay`; no receive-window credit, RFC rejection reason, exact exit metadata, or deep rekey/keepalive value is fabricated.
+
